7. AI VIDEO UNDERSTANDING PIPELINE
==================================================

This is the brain of ClipForge AI.

Implement the following stages.

STAGE 1: VIDEO INSPECTION

Use FFprobe or an equivalent verified media inspection method.

Extract:
- Video duration.
- Width and height.
- Frame rate.
- Audio availability.
- Video format.
- Resolution.

STAGE 2: AUDIO EXTRACTION

Use FFmpeg to extract audio.

Convert audio to a suitable format for transcription.

Recommended:
- Mono audio.
- 16 kHz sample rate.
- WAV or another supported format.

Handle videos with no audio gracefully.

STAGE 3: SPEECH TRANSCRIPTION

Use Gemini-supported audio processing or a compatible transcription integration.

Generate a timestamped transcript.

Each transcript segment must contain:

{
  "start": 0.0,
  "end": 5.5,
  "text": "Example spoken sentence",
  "speaker": null
}

Requirements:
- Preserve timestamps.
- Maintain original video time offsets.
- Handle longer recordings using chunks.
- Support English initially.
- Preserve other detected languages when possible.
- Never invent spoken words.

Allow users to inspect the transcript.

If exact speech recognition is uncertain, indicate that manual review may be needed.

STAGE 4: TRANSCRIPT CHUNKING

Divide the transcript into overlapping windows.

Suggested window duration:
30–90 seconds.

Ensure that each window preserves:
- Original timestamps.
- Complete sentences.
- Topic continuity.

STAGE 5: AI HIGHLIGHT DETECTION

Use Gemini to identify self-contained, valuable moments.

Look for:
- Strong opening hooks.
- Useful information.
- Interesting explanations.
- Questions and answers.
- Surprising facts.
- Personal stories.
- Important conclusions.
- Memorable statements.
- Educational takeaways.

Generate a maximum of five initial clip candidates.

Each candidate must contain:

{
  "start_time": 45.2,
  "end_time": 88.4,
  "title": "The Most Important Lesson",
  "hook": "An engaging opening line",
  "summary": "A short summary",
  "transcript_excerpt": "Exact words from the source transcript",
  "selection_reason": "Why this moment is valuable",
  "score": 87
}

Important:
- Start and end timestamps must be valid.
- Start and end should preserve complete thoughts.
- Do not cut sentences unnecessarily.
- Do not invent dialogue.
- Do not misrepresent the original speaker.
- Do not create unsupported claims.
- Reject invalid or overlapping duplicate candidates.

